      <p><strong>The Seven Sisters Waterfall</strong> is one of the best-known natural attractions of Geirangerfjord. It consists of seven separate streams cascading almost 250 metres down a steep cliff directly into the fjord. Its distinctive appearance has made it one of the symbols of western Norway.</p>

