      <p><strong>Trollstigen</strong>, meaning the <strong>Troll's Ladder</strong>, is one of Norway's most famous mountain roads. It crosses a high mountain pass in Møre og Romsdal County, linking the Romsdal Valley with the Geirangerfjord region. The route is celebrated for its steep climbs, sharp bends and breathtaking scenery.</p>

